{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1452, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given N strings S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_N, each consisting of lowercase English letters. The lengths of these strings are all distinct.\nSort these strings in ascending order of length, and then concatenate them in that order to form a single string.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\r\nS_1\r\nS_2\r\n\\vdots\r\nS_N\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 2 \\leq N \\leq 50\n- N is an integer.\n- Each S_i is a string consisting of lowercase English letters with length between 1 and 50, inclusive.\n- If i \\neq j, the length of S_i is different from the length of S_j.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3\r\ntc\r\noder\r\na\n\nSample Output 1\n\natcoder\r\n\nWhen we sort (tc, oder, a) in ascending order of length, we get (a, tc, oder). Concatenating them in this order yields the string atcoder.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4\r\ncat\r\nenate\r\non\r\nc\n\nSample Output 2\n\nconcatenate\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1498, "char_start": 1464, "quote": "Input:\n3\ntc\noder\na\nOutput:\natcoder", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1553, "char_start": 1510, "quote": "Input:\n4\ncat\nenate\non\nc\nOutput:\nconcatenate", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "3ed8dd238346cf07afcdcbbac1441783740620d80107e1d541a61528e03cbae0", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "7298d37f1a7e93b8bd0a9945de83dd9ec86cd5653e15fd954c8052504e3e9d31", "seq": 2}
